/**
 * Longer descriptions compiled from each hospital's public website and other
 * public web sources. Figures that sources disagreed on are left out.
 */
export const hospitalOverviews: Record<string, string> = {
	'moolchand-hospital':
		"Moolchand Medcity is a multispeciality hospital group with facilities in South Delhi and Agra, and has been serving patients for around six decades. The South Delhi centre brings together 250+ doctors across 50+ specialities, including emergency care, cardiology, neurosciences, orthopaedics, renal care and dialysis, gastroenterology, paediatrics and a women's institute. It was among the first Indian hospitals to perform minimal access and laparoscopic surgery, and holds JCI, NABH, NABL and ISO accreditations.",
	'fortis-c-doc-hospital':
		"Fortis C-DOC is a compact, 23-bed centre of excellence for diabetes, metabolic disease and endocrinology, led by Prof. Anoop Misra and operating in this field since 2011. Its facilities include two operating suites, a diabetic foot and wound care centre, a diabetic eye lab and a dialysis centre. It also runs weight-management programmes with bariatric and minimal access surgery, backed by a 24/7 diagnostic laboratory, radiology and pharmacy.",
	'fortis-escorts-heart-institute':
		"Fortis Escorts Heart Institute is a 310-bed hospital known worldwide for cardiac sciences and celebrated 25 years of cardiac care in 2013. Its heart programme covers complex angioplasty, TAVR, pacing and electrophysiology, adult and paediatric cardiac surgery, minimally invasive and robotic surgery, LVAD and heart transplantation. The hospital also treats gastrointestinal, pancreatic and liver disorders, including liver transplants.",
	'fortis-flt-lt-rajan-dhall-hospital':
		"Fortis Flt. Lt. Rajan Dhall Hospital in Vasant Kunj is a 162+ bed multispeciality hospital in South Delhi, about 8 km from the international airport. It offers around 30 specialities, with dedicated centres for cardiac sciences, orthopaedics and joint replacement, renal sciences, oncology, rheumatology, pulmonology and critical care, and bariatric sciences. Specialised clinics cover asthma and allergy, kidney stones, obesity, sports injury and menopause.",
	'blk-max-super-speciality-hospital':
		"BLK-Max is one of the largest private tertiary-care hospitals in India, spread over five acres with a 650-bed capacity and a legacy dating back to 1959. It runs dedicated centres for cancer, bone marrow transplant, heart, neurosciences, digestive and liver diseases, renal sciences and kidney transplant, orthopaedics and joint replacement, chest diseases and critical care. It also has transplant programmes for bone marrow, liver, kidney and heart, and is accredited by JCI, NABH and NABL.",
	'artemis-hospital':
		"Artemis Hospital, founded by the Apollo Tyres Group and opened in 2007, is described as the first JCI-accredited hospital in Gurugram. The 600+ bed hospital sits on a 9-acre campus with specialists across 40+ disciplines, including cardiology, oncology, neurosciences, orthopaedics, nephrology, gastroenterology, urology and organ transplantation. Robotic-assisted surgery with the da Vinci system and neurosciences services such as Gamma Knife and deep brain stimulation are among its highlights.",
	'max-super-speciality-hospital-saket':
		"Max Super Speciality Hospital, Saket is a 514+ bed hospital in South Delhi, arranged as East and West blocks. It has 25 modular operation theatres, 170+ critical care beds, an advanced dialysis unit, an onco day-care unit and 680+ specialists across 32 specialities. Its centres cover cardiac care, oncology, transplants (heart, lung and bone marrow), minimal access and bariatric surgery, and it is accredited as a centre of excellence for bariatric and hernia surgery.",
	'indraprastha-apollo-hospitals':
		"Indraprastha Apollo Hospitals, opened in 1996, is the flagship Apollo hospital in Delhi, spread across 15 acres with 710 operational beds and 250+ ICU beds. It runs one of India's busiest liver and kidney transplant programmes, a bone marrow transplant unit, and multi-organ transplants including heart, pancreas and paediatric cases. The comprehensive cancer centre offers HDR brachytherapy and tomotherapy alongside India's first proton therapy centre, and the hospital uses the da Vinci robotic surgery system.",
	'apollo-spectra-hospitals':
		"Apollo Spectra Delhi operates two centres, in Karol Bagh and Chirag Enclave, focused on surgical and day-care specialities. Its services include general and laparoscopic surgery, orthopaedics and spine, urology, varicose veins, bariatric surgery, gynaecology and ENT. Each centre has modern modular operation theatres, an endoscopy suite, a critical care unit, in-house pharmacy, diagnostics and radiology, supported by around 60 specialist consultants.",
	'batra-hospital-medical-research-centre':
		"Batra Hospital & Medical Research Centre was established in 1987 as Delhi's first private multispeciality hospital and was inaugurated by then Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi. It grew into a 500-bed tertiary-care hospital with 14 operating theatres, about 110 ICU beds and 24/7 emergency services across 42 specialities. It set up some of the earliest private-sector centres of excellence in oncology, cardiology and nephrology, along with neurosciences, gastroenterology and renal transplantation.",
	'aakash-healthcare-super-speciality-hospital':
		"Aakash Healthcare, founded in 2011 in Dwarka, is a 230-bed tertiary-care hospital with 70 critical care beds and 15 dialysis stations. It is particularly known for orthopaedics and joint replacement, and runs centres of excellence in cardiology, general and minimal access surgery, ophthalmology and refractive surgery, mother and child care, neurosciences and renal sciences. The hospital is NABH and NABL accredited and is empanelled under CGHS.",
	'manipal-hospital-dwarka':
		"Manipal Hospital Dwarka is a multi-super speciality tertiary-care hospital serving West Delhi, with 13 modular operation theatres and 118 critical care beds. Its centres of excellence cover orthopaedics and joint replacement, renal sciences, cardiac sciences, gastroenterology, neurosciences, oncology, and gynaecology and paediatrics, with dedicated liver transplantation and cancer care. Technology includes robotic surgery, O-arm imaging, telemedicine and electronic medical records, and the hospital holds NABH and NABL accreditation.",
	'sir-ganga-ram-hospital':
		"Sir Ganga Ram Hospital, named after the engineer and philanthropist Sir Ganga Ram, has served Delhi since 1954 and has around 675 beds. Its departments include cardiology and the Dharma Vira Heart Centre, oncology, gastroenterology, orthopaedics, neurology, genetic medicine, minimal access and bariatric surgery, liver transplantation and cochlear implants. The nephrology department began in 1981 and the first kidney transplant was performed in 1987; roughly 250 transplants are now performed each year.",
	'amrita-hospital':
		"Amrita Hospital in Faridabad opened in August 2022 as a 2,600-bed tertiary, multispeciality and super-speciality hospital. It has eight centres of excellence covering cancer care, cardiac sciences, neurosciences, digestive diseases, orthopaedics and joint replacement, renal sciences, solid organ transplantation, and mother and child care. It has 534 AI-monitored critical care beds, advanced imaging including PET-CT and 3T MRI, and is recognised for robotic liver donor surgery.",
	'metro-heart-institute-with-multispeciality':
		"Metro Heart Institute in Faridabad has operated since 2002 as Haryana's first dedicated heart hospital, and today has 400+ beds and over 30 specialities. Its cardiac team has performed more than 75,000 angiographies and angioplasties and over 10,000 cardiac surgeries, and it introduced TAVI and minimally invasive heart surgery to the region. The hospital also offers kidney transplantation, bone marrow transplantation and mammography, and holds NABH and NABL accreditation.",
	'the-sight-avenue':
		"The Sight Avenue is a super-speciality eye hospital founded by Dr. Suraj Munjal, with centres in Greater Kailash, New Delhi and Sector 38, Gurugram. It offers cataract surgery including bladeless laser techniques, LASIK, Contoura Vision, SMILE, implantable collamer lenses, retina and uvea care, glaucoma, cornea and keratoconus, squint, oculoplasty and paediatric ophthalmology. The hospital reports having treated more than 50,000 patients.",
	'shroff-eye-centre':
		"Shroff Eye Centre provides complete eye care from centres in Kailash Colony and Connaught Place, with Dr. Cyrus Shroff on the team since 1984. It offers stitchless phacoemulsification cataract surgery with premium lenses, refractive surgery including LASIK, Femto Contoura, SILK, ICL and PRK, vitreo-retinal surgery, cornea and glaucoma care, paediatric ophthalmology and a dedicated dry eye clinic. As a tertiary eye centre it handles over 10,000 surgeries a year.",
	'eye7-hospitals':
		"Eye7 Eye Hospitals is a network of eye-care centres across Delhi-NCR with over 30 years of practice and more than 200,000 cumulative surgeries. Its services include Contoura Vision and bladeless femtosecond LASIK, EVO ICL, refractive lens exchange, cataract, glaucoma, retina, cornea, squint, neuro-ophthalmology, oculoplasty, paediatric ophthalmology and low vision. The hospitals are NABH accredited and are on the panels of CGHS, ECHS and other government schemes.",
	'sharp-sight-eye-hospitals':
		"Sharp Sight Eye Hospitals, established in 1998, is a chain of eye-care centres across North India that is NABH accredited and CGHS endorsed. It provides cataract surgery using conventional and advanced laser techniques, bladeless LASIK, glaucoma care, squint and lazy-eye treatment, diabetic retinopathy care, cornea services and paediatric ophthalmology. Retina diagnostics such as FFA, B-scan ultrasound and OCT support its retinal surgeons.",
	'venu-eye-institute-research-centre':
		"Venu Eye Institute & Research Centre is an eye hospital on a 2.5-acre campus in Sheikh Sarai, South Delhi, providing OPD and inpatient care for both paying and subsidised patients under one roof. Services include cataract and refractive surgery, LASIK, cornea, glaucoma and retina treatment, oculoplasty, orbital tumour surgery, squint surgery and contact lens services. Over more than 40 years it has treated millions of patients, many of them free of cost or at subsidised rates, and it also trains ophthalmic professionals.",
	'guru-nanak-eye-centre':
		"Guru Nanak Eye Centre is a Delhi government ophthalmic institute conceived in 1971, with its outpatient block operational since 1977. It has six ophthalmic units, indoor wards and operation theatres, and runs super-speciality clinics for cornea, retina, glaucoma, neuro-ophthalmology, paediatric ophthalmology, squint and contact lenses. Outpatient services are provided free of cost, with a large team of ophthalmologists seeing patients every day.",
	'shining-smile-dentistry':
		"Shining Smiles Dentistry in Saket, New Delhi, opened in 2021 and is known for dental implants, immediate implants and smile makeovers. Its services include Hollywood smile design, digital smile design, veneers, Invisalign, crowns, sinus lift and bone grafting, and microscopic root canal treatment. Treatment rooms use digital X-rays, 3D scanners and intraoral cameras for precise diagnosis and planning.",
	'spruce-dental-chain-of-clinics':
		"Spruce Dental Chain of Clinics, led by Dr. Javed Rizwan, is a dental implant and orthodontics practice behind Medanta Hospital in Gurugram, also known as Smile Garden Dental Implant Center. It offers immediate and conventional implants using titanium or zirconia, root canal treatment, smile design, braces and aligners, and full-mouth rehabilitation. Dr. Rizwan has over 20 years of experience and a Master's in Strategic Implantology from Germany.",
	'dr-agarwal-s-eye-hospital':
		"Dr. Agarwal's Eye Hospital was founded in 1957 in Chennai by Padma Bhushan Dr. Jaiveer Agarwal and Dr. Tahira Agarwal, and has grown into one of India's largest eye-care chains, with centres across many Indian states and overseas. It provides cataract surgery including femtosecond laser-assisted techniques, LASIK and other refractive surgery, retina care for conditions such as diabetic retinopathy and retinal detachment, glaucoma, cornea and paediatric ophthalmology, and operates several centres in Delhi-NCR.",
	'asg-eye-hospital':
		"ASG Eye Hospital is a chain of super-speciality eye hospitals founded in 2005 in Jodhpur by Dr. Arun Singhvi and Dr. Shilpi Gang, and now present across many cities in India. Its Noida centre treats cataract with premium lenses, LASIK including Contoura and PRK, glaucoma, retinal diseases including diabetic retinopathy, cornea, squint, oculoplasty, paediatric and neuro-ophthalmology, all under one roof.",
	'eye-q-super-speciality-eye-hospitals':
		"Eye-Q began in 2007 as a single facility and has grown into a super-speciality eye hospital chain across North India, with several centres in Gurugram including Golf Course Road and DLF Cyber City. Services include bladeless laser cataract surgery, LASIK, retina care with laser photocoagulation and cryopexy, glaucoma, oculoplasty, neuro-ophthalmology, squint and in-house opticals and pharmacy.",
	'medanta-the-medicity':
		"Medanta – The Medicity, founded by cardiac surgeon Dr. Naresh Trehan in 2009, is one of India's largest multi-super speciality hospitals, with 29 super-speciality units and 800+ doctors. Its six centres of excellence cover cardiac sciences, neurosciences, bone and joint, cancer, renal and urology, and liver transplantation. It reports over 500 living-donor liver transplants, uses the da Vinci robotic system, and is ranked India's top private hospital in Newsweek's World's Best Hospitals.",
	'fortis-memorial-research-institute-fmri':
		"Fortis Memorial Research Institute is a multi-super speciality, quaternary-care hospital near HUDA City Centre in Gurugram, accredited by JCI, NABH and NABL. Its centres of excellence include robotic surgery, oncology, cardiology and cardiac surgery, kidney and liver transplants, haematology and bone marrow transplant, gastroenterology, neurosciences, urology, orthopaedics and joint replacement, and bariatric surgery. More than 2,500 bone marrow transplants have been performed here.",
	'sanar-international-hospitals':
		"Sanar International Hospitals, now Shalby Sanar International Hospital, is a multispeciality hospital on Golf Course Road, Gurugram, accredited by JCI and NABH. It offers cancer care, heart care, bone marrow, kidney and liver transplants, and is best known for orthopaedics and joint replacement, backed by the Shalby group's experience of more than 150,000 joint replacements. The team also performs revision hip and knee surgery using computer navigation and special implants.",
	'jaypee-hospital':
		"Jaypee Hospital is the Jaypee Group's flagship tertiary-care hospital on a 25-acre campus in Sector 128, Noida, with 525+ operational beds, 150+ ICU beds and 18 modular operation theatres. It offers 30+ super-specialities, including a heart institute with hybrid cath labs and an institute for organ transplants covering liver, kidney, heart, cornea and bone marrow, supported by a 12-bed transplant ICU. Robotic surgery with the da Vinci system is available for urology, gynaecology and general surgery.",
	'marengo-asia-hospitals':
		"Marengo Asia Hospitals in Faridabad, formerly QRG Health City, is a 450-bed multi-super-specialty tertiary-care hospital established in 2007 and accredited by NABH and NABL. Its specialities include oncology, cardiac sciences, gastroenterology, liver transplant and biliary sciences, orthopaedics and joint replacement, bone marrow transplant, renal sciences and neurosciences. Diagnostic and imaging facilities include MRI, CT and endoscopic ultrasound.",
	'marengo-asia-hospitals-gurugram':
		"Marengo Asia Hospitals in Gurugram, formerly W Pratiksha Hospital, is a multispeciality tertiary and quaternary-care hospital with around 250 beds, accredited by NABH and NABL. It covers 21+ specialities including cardiology, neurology, orthopaedics, urology, oncology, fertility, women's health and critical care. The Marengo Asia International Institute of Neuro & Spine is its centre of excellence, with robotic-assisted spine surgery, and the hospital reports over 6,000 joint replacements and 5,500 IVF procedures.",
	'fortis-hospital':
		"Fortis Hospital, Noida, founded in 2004, is a multi-specialty tertiary-care hospital with 12 operation theatres and NABH accreditation. Its cardiac centre offers ECMO, TAVI, LVAD, heart transplantation and complex surgery supported by twin cath labs, while its neurosciences and orthopaedics departments use neuro-navigation and keyhole spine surgery. It also runs kidney and liver transplant programmes and services in oncology, gastroenterology, urology and emergency trauma care.",
	'fortis-hospital-shalimar-bagh':
		"Fortis Hospital, Shalimar Bagh, opened in 2010, is a 262-bed multi-super-speciality hospital on a 7.34-acre campus, accredited by NABH and NABL. Its centres of excellence cover critical care, emergency and trauma, neurosciences, bone and joint, cardiac sciences and gastro sciences, and it offers kidney transplant, obstetrics, and neonatology with a Level III NICU. Robotic surgery and a certified bariatric surgery centre are among its highlights, and it is India's first hospital registered under the Green Building Rating System.",
	'fortis-hospital-faridabad':
		"Fortis Escorts Hospital, Faridabad, began in 1982 as Escorts Heart Institute and Research Centre and joined Fortis Healthcare in 2005. It offers a full range of cardiac services, from interventional cardiology with TAVI and atherectomy to open-heart surgery and heart transplantation. Other services include neurosciences, orthopaedics, urology, nephrology, gastroenterology, critical care and organ transplants. It was the first hospital in the city to receive NABH accreditation.",
	'max-hospital':
		"Max Super Speciality Hospital, Gurugram, near HUDA City Centre in Sector 43, is a compact superspeciality hospital accredited by NABH and NABL. It provides medical and surgical oncology, cardiology, orthopaedics and joint replacement, nephrology, neurosciences, urology, minimal access surgery, obstetrics and gynaecology, paediatrics, IVF and critical care. Its ICUs include 12 adult ICU beds, PICU, NICU and cardiac care beds, supported by endoscopy, radiology and pathology.",
	'max-super-speciality-hospital-vaishali':
		"Max Super Speciality Hospital, Vaishali, in Ghaziabad, is a 387+ bed hospital with 128 critical care beds, 16 high-dependency beds and 14 modular operation theatres. It offers 37+ clinical specialities and houses institutes for neurosciences, renal sciences, cancer care and cardiac sciences, plus a trauma centre and kidney and liver transplant services. The hospital is accredited by NABH and NABL.",
	'max-super-speciality-hospital-noida':
		"Max Healthcare's Noida hospitals are among the more advanced multispeciality hospitals in the Delhi-NCR region, known for cardiac sciences, oncology, neurosciences, orthopaedics, gastroenterology and renal care. The larger Sector 128 flagship has 500+ beds with plans to expand to 1,200, and its technology includes the da Vinci Xi robotic system, a TrueBeam linear accelerator, 3T MRI and PET-CT. The hospitals are NABH accredited.",
	'max-super-speciality-hospital-dwarka':
		"Max Super Speciality Hospital, Dwarka, is a 300+ bed tertiary-care hospital on an 8.62-acre eco-friendly campus, one of Delhi NCR's first five-star GRIHA-rated green hospitals. It has 120+ critical care beds, 10 modular operation theatres, a dedicated chemotherapy wing and a busy emergency department. Specialities include cardiac, neuro, renal, liver and gastro sciences, oncology, orthopaedics, bariatric and robotic surgery, ENT and cochlear implants, and IVF, with the da Vinci robot and a 3T MRI on site.",
	'max-super-speciality-hospital-shalimar-bagh':
		"Max Super Speciality Hospital, Shalimar Bagh, established in 2011, is a large multi-super speciality hospital in North West Delhi accredited by JCI and NABH. It offers 37+ clinical specialities including cancer care, cardiac sciences, neurosciences, gastroenterology, orthopaedics, nephrology and urology, and is known for its comprehensive treatment for complex conditions under one roof.",
	'max-smart-super-speciality-hospital':
		"Max Smart Super Speciality Hospital is a 250-bed tertiary-care hospital in the Saket Institutional Area with about 50 critical care beds and 12 modular operation theatres. It is a referral centre for neurovascular intervention, targeted cancer therapy, cardiac and orthopaedic surgery, and liver and kidney transplants. Technology includes 3T MRI, 256-slice CT angiography, the Mako robotic arm for joint replacement and the da Vinci Xi system, and the hospital is NABH accredited.",
	'psri-hospital':
		"Pushpawati Singhania Hospital & Research Institute, established in 1996 by two AIIMS professors, is a multispeciality hospital in Sheikh Sarai, South Delhi, accredited by JCI and NABH. Its super-specialities include cardiology and cardiothoracic surgery, neurosciences, gastroenterology, liver and kidney transplant programmes, orthopaedics and joint replacement, nephrology, urology, pulmonology and sleep medicine, and oncology. It is especially known for care of the liver, kidney, prostate, gall bladder, pancreas and gastrointestinal tract.",
	'venkateshwar-hospital':
		"Venkateshwar Hospital, established in 2016 in Dwarka, is a NABH and NABL-accredited tertiary-care hospital with 125 ICU beds and 10 modular operation theatres. It covers 34+ specialities, with centres of excellence in cardiac sciences, oncology and bone marrow transplant, renal sciences, neurosciences, and gastro sciences with liver transplantation. Technology includes the Hugo robotic-assisted surgery system, 3T MRI, 256-slice CT, PET-CT, cath labs and linear accelerators.",
	'primus-super-speciality-hospital':
		"Primus Super Speciality Hospital, in the diplomatic enclave of Chanakyapuri, is a 250-bed NABH-accredited hospital that performs more than 3,300 surgeries a year. It offers orthopaedics, oncology, gastroenterology, cardiology, nephrology, neurosciences, transplant and urology, with specialised spine and orthopaedic, minimal access surgery, and neurology and neurosurgery centres. Facilities include seven modular operation theatres, a flat-panel cath lab and a 15-bed dialysis unit.",
	'ck-birla-hospital':
		"CK Birla Hospital in Punjabi Bagh, part of the CK Birla Group and opened in 2021, is a 230+ bed multi-specialty hospital in West Delhi accredited by NABH and NABL. It has strong mother-and-child services, including obstetrics, a Level III NICU, fetal medicine, fertility and IVF, and North India's first water-birthing facility. It also offers oncology, orthopaedics and spine, and advanced surgical sciences, with robotic surgery in orthopaedics, urology and gynaecology.",
	'narayana-hospital':
		"Narayana Superspeciality Hospital in Gurugram belongs to the Narayana Health group, founded by cardiac surgeon Dr. Devi Shetty, and has 215 beds and NABH accreditation. It is particularly strong in cardiac sciences, offering ECMO, TAVI, CRT, heart transplant, minimally invasive and robotic cardiac surgery, and advanced angioplasty. The group also runs centres of excellence in cancer care, neurosciences, orthopaedics, gastro sciences and renal sciences.",
	'asian-institute-of-medical-sciences':
		"Asian Institute of Medical Sciences, established in 2010, is a 425-bed tertiary-care hospital in Faridabad accredited by NABH, NABL and AACI. It runs 14 centres of excellence, including the Asian Cancer Centre, which was the first in North India to deploy Varian RapidArc on a Trilogy system, and a bone marrow transplant centre for blood cancers and non-malignant conditions. Other strengths include cardiology and cardiac surgery, orthopaedics and spine, neurosciences, renal transplant and gastroenterology.",
	'yatharth-super-speciality-hospital':
		"Yatharth Super Speciality Hospital in Noida Extension, established in 2010, is a 450-bed tertiary-care hospital with 125 critical care beds and 11 modular operation theatres. It is described as the first and only hospital in Uttar Pradesh with JCI accreditation, and is also NABH accredited. Centres of excellence include cardiology, oncology, neurosciences, urology, nephrology, gastroenterology, and spine and rheumatology, and the hospital offers robotic surgery with the da Vinci X system.",
	'yashoda-super-speciality-hospitals':
		"Yashoda Super Speciality Hospital in Kaushambi, Ghaziabad, became operational in 2006 with 100 beds and now has around 300, with NABH and NABL accreditation. It offers advanced care across 50+ specialities, including neurosciences, cardiology and cardiothoracic surgery, joint replacement, paediatrics, nephrology and renal transplant, and gastroenterology. A cancer care programme adds palliative care, pain management, physiotherapy, nutrition counselling and psychological support.",
	'saroj-super-speciality-hospital':
		"Saroj Super Speciality Hospital in Rohini has operated since 1997 as a 154+ bed multi-super speciality hospital in North-West Delhi, and began as a heart institute inaugurated in 2001 by President K. R. Narayanan. It offers cardiac surgery, neurology and neurosurgery, nephrology, joint replacement, minimal access surgery, gastroenterology, cancer care, and plastic and reconstructive surgery, supported by advanced cath labs and multi-slice CT. It is accredited by NABH and NABL, open 24 hours and on the panel of 100+ insurers and organisations.",
	'aakash-hospital':
		"Aakash Hospital in Malviya Nagar, founded in 2004, is a 50-bed multi-speciality hospital in South Delhi that is NABH accredited and ISO 9001 certified. It provides internal medicine, general and orthopaedic surgery, obstetrics and gynaecology, paediatrics and neonatology, ENT, gastroenterology, pulmonology, dermatology and critical care. Emergency services run 24 hours a day, and patients can choose deluxe, air-conditioned or economy rooms, with oxygen and suction pipelines beside each bed.",
	'sci-international-hospital':
		"SCI International Hospital, founded in 2014 in Greater Kailash Part 1, is a 50-bed NABH-accredited super-speciality surgical centre with four modular operation theatres and 15 critical care beds. It is a centre of excellence for urology and andrology, IVF and fertility, gynaecology and obstetrics, advanced laparoscopic surgery, orthopaedics, joint replacement and sports injury, ENT and cochlear implants, and neonatology. Ophthalmology and dentistry are also available.",
	'the-signature-advanced-super-speciality-hospital':
		"The Signature Advanced Super Speciality Hospital, established in 2019 under the Park Hospital network, is a 150-bed NABH-accredited hospital near the Dwarka Expressway in Sector 37D, Gurugram. It offers cardiac sciences, orthopaedics and joint replacement, neurosciences, gastroenterology, renal sciences and kidney transplant, obstetrics and gynaecology, paediatrics, ENT, ophthalmology and interventional radiology. MRI, CT, laboratories and a blood bank support 24x7 emergency care.",
	'sci-ivf-hospital':
		"SCI IVF Hospital is a fertility centre in Greater Kailash, Delhi, founded by Dr. Shivani Sachdev Gour and Dr. Vishal Dutt Gour and part of SCI Healthcare. It offers IVF, ICSI, IUI, egg freezing, donor programmes and genetic testing for both male and female infertility, supported by an in-house embryology laboratory. Dr. Gour trained as a clinical research fellow in IVF at Hammersmith Hospital in London and became a member of the Royal College of Obstetricians and Gynaecologists (UK) in 2005.",
	'nova-ivf-fertility':
		"Nova IVF Fertility, established in 2011, is a chain of fertility centres across major Indian cities, including several clinics in Delhi NCR, in partnership with IVI of Spain. Services include IUI, IVF and ICSI, andrology, vitrification of eggs and embryos, assisted hatching, blastocyst culture and ERA testing. It introduced Delhi's first IVF centre with embryoscope time-lapse technology, which allows non-invasive monitoring of embryo growth to help select the best embryos.",
	'fortis-ridge-ivf-centre':
		"Fortis Ridge IVF Centre operates within Fortis Hospital, Shalimar Bagh, and has been providing fertility care since 2010. It offers IVF, ICSI and IUI, blastocyst transfer, preimplantation genetic testing, embryo freezing and fertility preservation programmes. A team of about 20 doctors, embryologists, andrologists, urologists, gynaecologists and psychologists provides complete male and female infertility treatment.",
	'delhi-ivf-fertility-research-centre':
		"Delhi IVF & Fertility Research Centre, founded by Dr. Anoop Gupta, is among India's earliest IVF clinics and has treated infertility since 1993 in Delhi. It offers IVF-ET, IUI, ICSI, assisted hatching, blastocyst culture and egg and embryo donation, backed by an advanced embryology laboratory. The centre states that it has helped over 21,000 couples from more than 66 countries, and provides coordinators for international patients with visa, accommodation and translation support.",
	'indira-ivf':
		"Indira IVF was founded in 2011 in Udaipur by Dr. Ajay Murdia and has grown into one of India's largest IVF chains, with over 100 centres nationwide, including Delhi and NCR. Each centre has its own embryology laboratory, specialist team and the full range of fertility diagnostics and treatments, including IUI, IVF and ICSI. The group says that it has helped more than 200,000 couples and has a team of 340+ IVF doctors.",
	'cloudnine-ivf-centre-kailash-colony':
		"Cloudnine Fertility in Kailash Colony is part of the Cloudnine group, which also provides maternity, gynaecology, paediatric and NICU care. The NABH-accredited centre offers IVF, ICSI, IVF with donor eggs, frozen embryo transfer, egg freezing and preimplantation genetic testing, along with counselling for the emotional side of treatment. International patient services include visa assistance, interpreters and travel coordination, and 24/7 emergency support is available.",
	'international-fertility-centre':
		"International Fertility Centre, headquartered in New Delhi and led by founder Dr. Rita Bakshi, is one of India's oldest fertility clinics and a network of 10+ IVF clinics in India and Nepal. Its Green Park centre offers IVF, ICSI, IUI, egg and sperm donation, PGD/PGS and endoscopy for women's health. Dr. Bakshi has more than 37 years of experience as an infertility specialist, and the centre performs over 1,000 IVF and ICSI cycles a year at its head office.",
	'laimaa-fertility-ivf-surrogacy-clinic':
		"Laimaa Fertility, established in 2022, is a fertility clinic in Greater Kailash Part II founded by embryologist Pooja Agarwal together with doctors Akanksha Chauhan and Mamta Chahar. It offers IVF, ICSI, IUI, egg and embryo freezing, egg donation and surgical solutions for infertility, and is known for handling complex cases such as low AMH and severe male-factor infertility. Its embryology work includes TESA-ICSI, PICSI, blastocyst transfer and embryo biopsy.",
	'gaudium-ivf':
		"Gaudium IVF and Women Health was founded in 2009 by infertility specialist and laparoscopic surgeon Dr. Manika Khanna and now has around 36 centres across six Indian states, including South Extension in Delhi. It offers IVF, egg and embryo freezing and treatment for recurrent IVF failure, male-factor infertility and endometriosis. Its embryology laboratory uses AI-assisted tools, including SiD for sperm assessment and ERICA for embryo evaluation.",
	'pristyn-care-ferticity-super-speciality-ivf-hospital':
		"Pristyn Care Ferticity Super Speciality & IVF Hospital in Malviya Nagar offers IVF, IUI, ICSI, egg and embryo freezing and donor-based treatments for couples. It manages PCOS, tubal block, low ovarian reserve, male-factor infertility, endometriosis and recurrent pregnancy loss, and also provides ovulation induction and detailed hormonal assessments. The clinic is listed in the ICMR ART Clinics Registry, and co-founder Dr. Ila Gupta has more than 29 years of experience.",
	'nova-ivf-fertility-centre-rajouri-garden':
		"Nova IVF Fertility's Rajouri Garden centre is one of the group's clinics in West Delhi and is open Monday to Saturday. It treats male infertility, unexplained infertility, low ovarian reserve, PCOS, endometriosis and tubal-factor infertility using IUI, IVF, ICSI and MACS sperm selection. Doctors here include Dr. Aswati Nair, a gynaecologist and IVF specialist with more than 17 years of experience in endometriosis, recurrent IVF failure and recurrent pregnancy loss.",
	'elixir-fertility-centre':
		"Elixir Fertility Centre, established in 2014, is a fertility clinic in Gujranwala Town in North Delhi. It offers IVF, ICSI, IUI and semen analysis, with an in-house diagnostic laboratory and ultrasound. The team includes Dr. Puneet Kochhar, a gynaecologist and IVF specialist who has worked at Bourn Hall Clinic in Cambridge, UK and held a teaching post at Lady Hardinge Medical College, Delhi.",
	'femmenest-fertility-ivf-centre':
		"Femmenest is a women's healthcare and fertility centre in Anand Vihar, East Delhi, offering IVF, IUI, ICSI and personalised fertility support for couples. It also provides gynaecology care for PCOS, hormonal imbalances and routine women's health check-ups, with diagnosis, hormonal therapies and complete infertility care in one place. The team includes fertility doctors, clinical embryologists and dedicated nursing staff, and the clinic is open six days a week and on Sunday mornings.",
	'india-ivf-clinic':
		"India IVF Clinic in Vasant Vihar is a fertility clinic that is part of the Fortis network, with a consulting presence at Fortis Flt. Lt. Rajan Dhall Hospital in Vasant Kunj. It offers IVF and fertility-enhancing surgery, with the team led by fertility specialists such as Dr. Richika Sahay. Patients rate it well for supportive staff and personal attention, and the clinic is wheelchair accessible with parking.",
	'spruce-dental':
		"Spruce Dental in Jasola Vihar is a South Delhi dental clinic providing pain-free root canal therapy, single-tooth and full-mouth dental implants, teeth whitening, orthodontic options and smile makeovers. Digital imaging is used for accurate diagnosis and treatment planning. The clinic is part of the Spruce Dental group led by implantologist and orthodontist Dr. Javed Rizwan.",
	'zemya-ivf-fertility-clinics':
		"Zemya IVF & Fertility Clinics in Green Park Extension provides IVF, IUI, ICSI, male infertility care, egg freezing and fertility preservation under one roof. The centre has modular operation theatres, a modern IVF laboratory, an advanced andrology laboratory, a pathology laboratory, a pharmacy and an international patients' lounge, with video consultations available. Its team of globally trained fertility specialists and ESHRE-certified embryologists reports having helped over 50,000 couples.",
	'kokilaben-dhirubhai-ambani-hospital':
		"Kokilaben Dhirubhai Ambani Hospital in Andheri West, Mumbai, began operations in 2009 as a 750-bed multi-speciality hospital with around 180 ICU beds, accredited by JCI, NABH and CAP. Its Centre for Robotic Surgery, set up in 2012, now uses the da Vinci Xi and India's first Toumai robotic system across oncology, urology, gynaecology and gastrointestinal surgery. Advanced technology and centres of excellence are a focus of the hospital, which serves patients from across India and abroad.",
	'p-d-hinduja-hospital':
		"P. D. Hinduja Hospital was founded in 1951 by Parmanand Deepchand Hinduja in collaboration with Massachusetts General Hospital, and moved into its Mahim East Wing building in 1963. It is a multi-speciality tertiary-care hospital with 45+ specialities, 53 critical care beds and 19 day-care units, covering cardiology, oncology, neurology and orthopaedics among others. The hospital runs DNB courses in 26 specialities, nursing and allied health programmes, and collaborates with institutions such as Stanford University and Hôpitaux Universitaires de Genève.",
	'fortis-hospital-mulund':
		"Fortis Hospital, Mulund, opened in 2002, is a 400-bed multi-specialty quaternary-care hospital with a record of repeated JCI accreditation. It is recognised as the largest transplant facility in Maharashtra, performing kidney, liver, heart and bone marrow transplants, and is known for neurosciences, cardiac sciences, oncology, nephrology, urology and orthopaedics. Its emergency department and Level 1 trauma centre are NABH accredited, and oncology uses the Versa HD linear accelerator.",
	'jaslok-hospital':
		"Jaslok Hospital & Research Centre, founded by philanthropist Seth Lokoomal Chanrai and surgeon Shantilal Jamnadas Mehta, was inaugurated in 1973 by Prime Minister Indira Gandhi. It is one of the country's oldest tertiary-care trust hospitals, with 350+ beds, about 50 specialities and nearly 20 specialty clinics. It launched India's first private urology department and performed a first renal transplant, and is known for cardiology, neurology, orthopaedics, oncology, assisted reproduction and multi-organ transplantation.",
	'nanavati-max-super-speciality-hospital':
		"Nanavati Max Super Speciality Hospital in Vile Parle was inaugurated in 1950 by Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru and opened to patients in 1951. It has 350 beds, 55 speciality departments and over 350 consultants, with centres of excellence in cardiology, oncology, nephrology, orthopaedics, spine surgery, neurology, bariatrics and surgical gastroenterology. Its imaging centre includes a 3T MRI and a 64-slice PET-CT scanner, and the hospital is accredited by NABH and NABL.",
	'apollo-hospitals-greams-road':
		"Apollo Hospitals, Greams Road, opened in 1983 and is the original Apollo hospital, now a 550-bed facility with JCI and NABH accreditation. It has 12+ centres of excellence, including the Apollo Heart Institute, Institute of Liver Sciences, Institute of Neurosciences and Institute of Robotic Surgery, and high-volume transplant programmes for liver, kidney, heart and lung. Technology includes the da Vinci system and TrueBeam radiotherapy, and its proton therapy centre is described as India's first.",
	'miot-international':
		"MIOT International, the Madras Institute of Orthopaedics and Traumatology, was founded by Prof. P. V. A. Mohandas in February 1999 as a 70-bed hospital and has grown into a 1,000-bed quaternary-care campus with 63 specialities and 21 operation theatres. Its orthopaedics and joint replacement department has been ranked first in India by Outlook Health, and it also runs liver and bone marrow transplant centres, oncology, cardiac care and nephrology. It has welcomed patients from over 130 countries and is accredited by NABH and NABL.",
	'gleneagles-global-health-city':
		"Gleneagles Global Health City in Perumbakkam is a large multi-organ transplant and quaternary-care hospital on a 21-acre campus and part of IHH Healthcare, with 40+ specialities. It performs liver, kidney, heart, lung and bone marrow transplants, with over 500 liver transplants reported, and runs its liver programme in collaboration with King's College Hospital, London. Oncology, hepatology, neurosciences and trauma care are other areas of strength, and the hospital is NABH accredited.",
	'fortis-malar-hospital':
		"Fortis Malar Hospital in Adyar is a 180-bed multi-speciality tertiary-care hospital with 40+ specialities, formerly Malar Hospital and part of Fortis Healthcare since 2007. It is particularly known for cardiac care, spanning interventional, non-invasive and paediatric cardiology, cardiovascular surgery and a heart transplant programme that it reports as one of the largest in Asia. Neurology, neurosurgery, orthopaedics, nephrology, gastroenterology and urology are also offered, and the hospital is NABH accredited.",
	'kauvery-hospital':
		"Kauvery Hospital in Alwarpet is a 300-bed multispeciality hospital in central Chennai, part of the Kauvery group, with NABH accreditation. It has centres of excellence in cardiac sciences, neurosciences, gastroenterology, organ transplantation, orthopaedics and women's health, and the Kauvery Heart Institute handles complex angioplasty, hybrid bypass surgery and heart transplants. The Kauvery Institute of Robotic Surgery offers da Vinci robotic procedures across oncology, urology, colorectal, cardiac and liver surgery and kidney transplantation.",
	'manipal-hospital-old-airport-road':
		"Manipal Hospital, Old Airport Road, has served Bengaluru since 1991 and is the flagship of the Manipal Hospitals network, with 144 intensive care beds and 20 modular operation theatres. It offers 60+ super-specialities, with centres of excellence in oncology, cardiac sciences, neurosciences, gastroenterology, orthopaedics and organ transplants. Its multi-organ transplant programme covers kidney, liver, pancreas and heart, and it was an early adopter of robotic-assisted kidney transplantation in India. The hospital holds NABH and JCI accreditation.",
	'sakra-world-hospital':
		"Sakra World Hospital, launched in February 2014, is a 350-bed multi-super-specialty hospital in Bengaluru, a joint venture between Kirloskar, Toyota Tsusho and Secom Hospitals of Japan. It offers neurology, cardiology, orthopaedics, spine surgery, renal sciences, oncology, obstetrics and gynaecology, rehabilitation sciences and paediatrics, and is known for organ transplants. Nursing protocols blend Indian and Japanese practice, and imaging includes MRI, multidetector CT and digital X-ray.",
	'narayana-institute-of-cardiac-sciences':
		"Narayana Institute of Cardiac Sciences, commissioned in 2000 at NH Health City in Bommasandra by Dr. Devi Shetty, is the flagship heart hospital of Narayana Health and among the largest cardiac hospitals in the world. It has 19 cardiac operation theatres, including two robotic theatres, and eight cath labs including a hybrid lab. The hospital performs more than 40 cardiac surgeries a day, including around 16 paediatric heart operations, and is accredited by JCI and NABH.",
	'fortis-hospital-bannerghatta-road':
		"Fortis Hospital, Bannerghatta Road, is Fortis Healthcare's flagship hospital in South India, offering super-specialty tertiary care across 40 fields and reported to be the first in Karnataka to earn JCI accreditation. Its centres of excellence include cardiology and cardiac surgery, neurosciences, oncology, orthopaedics, organ transplant, gastroenterology, paediatrics and critical care. Oncology offers PET-CT, robotic cancer surgery and HIFU for prostate cancer, and the Fortis Institute of Robotic Surgery is a centre of excellence.",
	'aster-cmi-hospital':
		"Aster CMI Hospital, in Hebbal, Bengaluru, is part of Aster DM Healthcare and offers close to 500 beds from primary to quaternary care, accredited by NABH and NABL. Its centres of excellence include cardiac sciences, neurosciences, gastroenterology, integrated liver care, organ transplant, urology and nephrology, orthopaedics, women's health and child health. The Aster International Institute of Oncology offers proton beam therapy, robotic surgery and HIPEC, and the transplant programme performs robotic kidney transplants.",
	'apollo-hospitals-jubilee-hills':
		"Apollo Hospitals, Jubilee Hills, established in 1988, is the flagship Apollo hospital in Hyderabad and holds JCI, NABH and NABL accreditation. It runs 12 centres of excellence, including cardiac sciences with three cath labs and robotic cardiac surgery, a cancer centre with robotic onco-surgery, and neurosciences with an intraoperative MRI suite and spinal robotics. Its transplant team handles liver, kidney, heart and bone marrow transplants, backed by a haematology-oncology unit.",
	'continental-hospitals':
		"Continental Hospitals, founded in 2013 in Hyderabad's Financial District, is a 585-bed hospital with 50+ specialities across 18 floors, accredited by JCI, NABH and NABL. It is described as India's first LEED-qualified super-speciality hospital, with green operation theatres and Level 3 NICU and PICU. It is known for complex organ transplants, cardiac sciences, neurosciences, oncology and orthopaedics, and its surgeons performed India's first robot-assisted CABG in April 2023.",
	'yashoda-hospitals-somajiguda':
		"Yashoda Hospitals, Somajiguda, is the first hospital of the Yashoda group and started in 1994, with 400+ beds and NABH accreditation. Its centres of excellence include heart and CT surgery, neurosciences, cancer, liver and multi-organ transplants, bones and joints, nephrology, robotic sciences, spine surgery, mother and child care and fertility. Laboratory, diagnostics and pharmacy services run 24 hours a day.",
	'global-hospitals-hyderabad':
		"Gleneagles Global Hospitals in Lakdi-ka-pul, known as Global Hospitals, was the first Gleneagles Global hospital in Hyderabad and is part of the group founded in 1999 by Dr. K. Ravindranath. It is best known for liver, kidney, heart and lung transplants, and reports India's first successful split and auxiliary liver transplant. Its operation theatres support robotic and minimal access surgery, with specialised ICUs including a liver ICU and post-transplant unit.",
	'kims-hospitals-secunderabad':
		"KIMS Hospitals, Secunderabad, opened in 2004 as a flagship 1,000-bed tertiary and quaternary-care hospital under Dr. Bhaskar Rao Bollineni. It offers cardiology, gastroenterology and hepatology, neurosciences, organ transplantation, oncology, orthopaedics, urology, fertility and bariatric surgery. The transplant programme covers heart, lung, liver, kidney and bone marrow, with its first heart transplant in 2012 and 1,000 kidney transplant surgeries recorded by 2019, and it holds NABH accreditation.",
	'amrita-institute-of-medical-sciences-kochi':
		"Amrita Hospital in Kochi, formerly Amrita Institute of Medical Sciences, was founded in 1998 by Mata Amritanandamayi Devi (Amma) as a multi-specialty tertiary referral and teaching hospital. It has 29 speciality departments and 17 centres of excellence, with a large faculty and support staff, and serves over a million outpatients and around 70,000 inpatients a year. Its laboratories are NABL accredited and the hospital holds NABH accreditation.",
	'aster-medcity':
		"Aster Medcity in Cheranalloor, Kochi, is a large quaternary-care hospital set on a 40-acre campus on the backwaters, and the first JCI-accredited quaternary-care multispecialty hospital in Kerala. It has eight centres of excellence, including neurosciences, cardiac sciences, orthopaedics, oncology, gastroenterology, nephrology and urology, women's health, and multi-organ transplantation. Its minimal access robotic surgery programme with the da Vinci system reports more than 5,000 robotic-assisted surgeries.",
	'lakeshore-hospital':
		"VPS Lakeshore Hospital in Nettoor, Kochi, is a multi super-speciality hospital that began functioning as a multi-specialty hospital in 2003 and is NABH accredited. It offers 30+ clinical departments, including multi-organ transplantation, gastroenterology, joint replacement, cardiology and cardiovascular surgery, and neurology. Its nephrology and renal transplant department has performed over 1,600 transplants, and the hospital reports Kerala's first paediatric bone marrow transplant and first liver transplant.",
	'kims-health-kochi':
		"KIMS Health, Kochi, in Edappally, is the Kochi hospital of the KIMS group headquartered in Thiruvananthapuram, with 125 beds and about 25 departments. It offers outpatient and inpatient services with 24-hour laboratory, pharmacy, X-ray and ECG facilities, staffed by experienced consultants and trained nurses. The hospital is accredited by NABH and by the Australian Council on Healthcare Standards International.",
	'apollo-multispeciality-hospitals-kolkata':
		"Apollo Multispeciality Hospitals on Canal Circular Road, opened in 2003, is a 700-bed hospital with 50+ specialities and 33 centres of excellence, and is the only hospital in eastern India with JCI accreditation. Its centres include heart care, cancer care, orthopaedics, gastroenterology, neurosciences, transplants, robotics and emergency care. It brought complete robotic renal transplant to eastern India, with living-donor and cadaver transplant programmes.",
	'amri-hospitals-dhakuria':
		"AMRI Hospitals, Dhakuria, began in 1996 as a public-private venture with the Government of West Bengal and grew from outpatient services to a large multi-specialty hospital, now part of Manipal Hospitals after its 2023 acquisition of a majority stake. It is known for cardiac sciences, joint replacement, trauma care, IVF, maxillofacial surgery and plastic surgery, with emergency and critical care as a centre of excellence. Advanced imaging and radiotherapy include PET-CT, SPECT-CT, IMRT and VMAT, and the hospital is NABH accredited.",
	'fortis-hospital-anandapur':
		"Fortis Hospital, Anandapur, founded in 2011, is a 10-storey hospital on a 7-acre site with around 300 beds. It offers cardiology and cardiac surgery, neurosciences, orthopaedics, nephrology, urology, pulmonology, digestive care, and mother and child care, with specialist clinics for pulmonary hypertension and allergies. The heart centre has four cath labs, a 14-bed surgical ICU and a 20-bed coronary care unit, and the hospital holds NABH and NABL accreditation.",
	'medica-superspecialty-hospital':
		"Medica Superspecialty Hospital in Mukundapur, established in 2010, is a large tertiary-care hospital and among the most trusted in eastern India, with 18 departments and eight centres of excellence. Its services include cardiology and cardiac surgery, neurosciences, gastroenterology and liver diseases, nephrology, oncology, orthopaedics, paediatrics and neonatology, and one of the region's most advanced critical care units. It became eastern India's first official training centre for robotic surgery in 2022 and runs a NABL-accredited laboratory with a molecular lab.",
	'zydus-hospitals':
		"Zydus Hospitals, established in 2015 on the S.G. Highway, is a 550-bed super-speciality hospital across 16 floors, accredited by NABH and NABL. Its centres of excellence include IVF, joint replacement, cancer care, neurology and neurosurgery, cardiac surgery, kidney and liver transplant, and plastic surgery. The liver transplant programme is supported by a multidisciplinary team of over 20 specialists, and across its centres Zydus reports more than 430 kidney and 295 liver transplants.",
	'cims-hospital':
		"CIMS Hospital, now Marengo Asia CIMS Hospital, opened in 2010 off Science City Road in Ahmedabad and is a multi-super speciality green hospital accredited by JCI, NABH and NABL. Its specialities include cancer care, cardiac sciences, gastroenterology, liver transplant, orthopaedics and joint replacement, renal sciences, neurosciences, bone marrow transplant and bariatric surgery. Led in cardiac surgery by Dr. Dhiren Shah, Gujarat's first heart transplant surgeon, it has a dedicated transplant centre for heart, lung, liver, kidney and paediatric bone marrow transplants.",
	'sterling-hospital':
		"Sterling Hospital in Gurukul, Ahmedabad, is part of a network of private hospitals in Gujarat and was the first hospital in the state to be fully accredited by NABH, in 2009. It offers cardiac sciences, oncology (surgical, medical and radiation), critical care and pulmonology, gastroenterology and GI surgery, neurosciences and spine surgery, nephrology and urology, orthopaedics and joint replacement, and bariatric surgery. Its paediatric and neonatal ICUs are equipped with multi-parameter monitoring, ventilators and ECMO.",
	'shalby-hospitals':
		"Shalby Hospitals began in Ahmedabad in 1994 as a joint replacement centre started by Dr. Vikram I. Shah and has since grown into a multi-speciality hospital chain. The SG Highway hospital, founded in 2007 and accredited by NABH and NABL, is known worldwide for orthopaedics, with more than 150,000 joint replacements performed across the group. Dr. Shah's ZERO technique reduced the surgical time for a knee replacement to around 10 to 12 minutes.",
};
